{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>My husband will accompany me.</b> Until now I was tending two sons with two hands; and now that a third son has been born to him, my husband will need to help me tend them." "<b>Therefore he called his name Levi.</b> Jacob called his name, for the reasoning of his name depends on Jacob, as it is written: ״Now my husband will accompany me.״ And even though the reasoning of Zevulun's name also depends on Jacob, as it is written: ״My husband will dwell with me״ — yet she called him Zevulun. One may answer: because Jacob did not agree to her words, that his primary dwelling should be with her, but rather with Rachel, therefore she called him Zevulun."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:39.023199872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}